0. Config & Asset validation
    - yaml configs
        - must parse properly & unambiguously into a combined RTC, in a transparent manner in the system which does it
            - yielding complaints to a collector for any violation encountered
            - then attempting to bypass it, keeping process going, so as many complaints can be collected in the pass
            - shared configs must declare filesets they reference
            - pud configs must declare referenced filesets, not already declared by shared cfg
    - layout assets
        - must be able to contain that which the app wants to assign to them, else cause of complaint
    - content bearing assets
        - must exist, else cause of complaint 

