5. Add asset exists check to ingestion pipeline
    - the service uses the file adapter to get assetlist
        - one for pud, other for shared
    - the service then passes filelist, rtc and ec to a worker, who
        - looks at md resolvers, their filelists and files
            - if files by name exist in either of pud or shared filelist, then ok, else complain
        - looks at repo resolvers
            - all paths must exist in pud filelist
        - looks at manifest resolver
            - pud_fileset, same as repo resolver
            - shared_fileset, from shared filelist

5. Add asset exists check to ingestion pipeline
    [ ] 'content/asset_ingestion/validators/asset_validator.py': Create asset existence validator 'AssetValidator'
        - ephemeral class with no __init__ method
        - implement 'validate' accepting pud_pathlist, shared_pathlist, rtc, and collector
        - traverse rtc resolvers to verify asset existence:
            - for MultiDocResolver: verify files by name exist in pud_pathlist or shared_pathlist, else complain
            - for RepoContentResolver: verify fileset paths exist in pud_pathlist, else complain
            - for ManifestResolver: verify pud_fileset in pud_pathlist and shared_fileset in shared_pathlist, else complain
    [ ] 'content/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Integrate asset validation in runtime config pipeline
        - use file adapter get_files to retrieve pud_filelist and shared_filelist
        - invoke AssetValidator with rtc, filelists, and collector before returning
        - return collector and runtime config

